From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yugidraft <yugidraft@localhost>
Date: Fri, 3 Mar 2000 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] core: core seats for multi-duelist card rules (MPNthDuelist,
 MPSeat, MPSeatOf, MPBindSeat, global effect, Tag flag key)

Duel.MPNthDuelist(i) rebinds the scope to the i-th living duelist counting from the scope player (R1). i = 0 and the end
of every call put P, the bound opponent, the window and the seat bind back (scope_guard), also for a filter and after a
Lua error; a prompt in the function keeps the rebind (call_coroutine). The trap build aborts when a call ends normally
with a rebind open. Duel.MPSeat gives the real seat of a Lua player value (Tag: the team), Duel.MPSeatOf the controller
seat of a card, and Duel.MPBindSeat binds the Lua value 1 to a real seat (a dead seat, a seat of the own team or no seat
gives an empty other side, never another opponent). These are the seats for the 92 "each living duelist" cards (R1) and
the 108 per-seat-state cards (R2).

R2 core rule: a global effect (Effect.GlobalEffect, or an effect that a script registers in initial_effect with
Duel.RegisterEffect) belongs to no seat. Its scope folds nothing, so it sees the real rp, ep and tp. In Tag a player
flag effect (Duel.RegisterFlagEffect) counts for the team of its seat (get, label and reset match by team).

Every site is guarded with n_duelists > 2. With 2 duelists nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
