+// ---- F7 part P2: seats for the "each duelist" (R1) and "per seat state" (R2) cards. n > 2 only: at n == 2 and in Lua
+// that runs for no duelist these functions give the stock answer (a value that is its own seat, no rebind).
+// Duel.MPNthDuelist(i): i >= 1 rebinds the CURRENT scope to the i-th living duelist in turn order from the scope player
+// (i == 1: that player). P becomes that seat (Tag: the fold of the seat is its team), the bound opponent and the
+// MPBindSeat bind are cleared and the window is closed. Gives true and the seat; gives false (and changes nothing) for
+// an i past the last living duelist, below 1 or above MAX_DUELISTS. An eliminated duelist is skipped, the Tag partner
+// counts. The first rebind keeps the values of the scope (P0, bound, own_bound, bind, window); i == 0 puts them back
+// (true, also when nothing was rebound). A call that ends puts them back on every path (scope_guard), and a prompt in
+// the loop keeps the rebind (call_coroutine). The trap build aborts when a call ends normally with a rebind open.
+// "i" counts from P0 (the scope player before the first rebind), not from the duelist of the previous step.
+LUA_STATIC_FUNCTION(MPNthDuelist) {
